   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ עִיר שֶׁיֵּשׁ בָּהּ עֲבוֹדָה זָרָה, וְהָיוּ בָּהּ חֲנוּיוֹת מְעוּטָּרוֹת וְשֶׁאֵינָן מְעוּטָּרוֹת, זֶה הָיָה מַעֲשֶׂה בְּבֵית שְׁאָן, וְאָמְרוּ חֲכָמִים: הַמְעוּטָּרוֹת אֲסוּרוֹת, וְשֶׁאֵינָן מְעוּטָּרוֹת מוּתָּרוֹת.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» With regard to «a city in which idol worship» is practiced «and in which there are stores that are adorned» for the sake of idol worship «and» there are others «that are not adorned, this was» in fact «an incident» that occurred «in Beit She’an, and the Sages said:» With regard to «the adorned» shops, it is «prohibited» to buy from them, «but» in the case of «those that are not adorned» it is «permitted.»"
  }
